meta {
  name: Finish Service Execution
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/service-orders/{{serviceOrderId}}/services/{{serviceId}}/finish
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Finish Service Execution
  
  Marks a service as completed/finished within a service order. This records the finish time.
  
  ## Prerequisites
  - Valid JWT token in `jwtToken` variable
  - Service Order ID in `serviceOrderId` variable
  - Service ID in `serviceId` variable
  - Service must have been started first
  - User must be the same technician who started the service (or have override permissions)
  
  ## Path Parameters
  - `serviceOrderId` - UUID of the service order
  - `serviceId` - UUID of the service within the order
  
  ## Response
  Returns the updated service order with the service status changed to "FINISHED".
  
  ## Notes
  - Can only finish a service that has been started
  - Recording the finish time completes time tracking
  - May trigger downstream events (e.g., outbox messages, SQS notifications)
  - If all services are finished, the order status may automatically update
  
  ## Error Handling
  - 422: Service not started, already finished, or user permission denied
}
